Greetings ceph-sational humans,

As many of you have noticed we have relaunched the Ceph wiki for
general community use.  For now it is divided into five basic
categories (although these are also fluid):

http://wiki.ceph.com/

1) Planning :: for all things forward-looking. Links to roadmap plans,
blueprints (There is still time to submit blueprints for the Dumpling
planning summit.  Submit your blueprint ideas today!), or other things
to help lay out a concrete (and public) plan for Ceph development.

2) Guides :: just what you might expect.  Have a method for deploying
Ceph? Walkthrough of how you profile your Ceph cluster? All things
welcome!

3) FAQs :: a running tally of some of the more frequent knowledge
requests coming from places like word-of-mouth, irc, and here on the
lists.  Feel free to add your own.

4) Development :: this is for more general development ideas, napkin
sketches, and tools for Ceph development.

5) Community :: aggregation of useful information from, and for, the
community.  Can be used to plan meetups, keep track of Ceph in the
press, share etherpads, or anything you might be able to imagine.


This is back by popular demand, so feel free to make use of it!  If
you have questions, comments, or anything for the good of the cause
drop me or community@inktank.com a line.  Thanks.



